+## Optional peer review — transform key masked by symmetry
+
+A source-bound protected-Racket probe found a learnability defect in seed 5 with
+indices 0–2 used as demonstrations and index 3 as the query. The observed keys
+are `[5, 3, 2, 3]`. A rival that changes only `key 3` from clockwise rotation to
+identity matches all three demonstration outputs because the sole key-3
+demonstration template is clockwise-invariant. The same rival disagrees on the
+asymmetric key-3 query.
+
+Evidence: `checks/tickets/1aec632783b9/counterexample.json` and
+`rival-key3-identity.rkt`. The generator source is pinned at SHA-256
+`c55bcb365fd21c4da45afc5b8db7230501e7bbc0173c50872b7820b9a5e87505`.
+
+Recommended repair: when a query uses a transform key, require at least one
+visible demonstration with that key whose template distinguishes the canonical
+transform from the competing transforms; redraw or add a demonstration when
+symmetry masks the mapping. This review is one explicit rival on one lesson, not
+a full curriculum census. No production change was applied.
