 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Optional peer review — command 2 masked by source symmetry
+
+A source-bound protected-Racket probe found a learnability defect in seed 47 with
+indices 0–2 used as demonstrations and index 3 as the query. A rival that changes
+only command 2 from clockwise rotation to vertical reflection matches all three
+demonstration outputs: every demonstration source motif used with command 2 has
+`rotate-cw(source) == flip-ud(source)`. The query contains command 2 on an
+asymmetric source motif, so the rival and canonical programs disagree.
+
+Evidence: `checks/tickets/ffc1598119d4/counterexample.json` and
+`rival-code2-flipud.rkt`. The generator source is pinned at SHA-256
+`1d6b558856708e60097802e84857ad51b971217a9651e7ea038e6bbbb448a3c4`.
+
+Recommended repair: for every transform code used by a query, require a visible
+demonstration whose source motif separates that transform from each competitor;
+redraw the lesson or add a demonstration when a symmetry hides the distinction.
+This review is one explicit rival on one lesson, not a full curriculum census.
+No production change was applied.
